{"title":"Career Roadmap · Regulatory Affairs Executive","role":"Regulatory Affairs Executive","summary":"A Regulatory Affairs Executive helps pharmaceutical, biotechnology, medical-device, nutraceutical, and healthcare-product organizations ensure that products comply with applicable regulatory requirements throughout their lifecycle.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Pharm (Bachelor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Pharmaceutical Sciences"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Regulatory Affairs Executive helps pharmaceutical, biotechnology, medical-device, nutraceutical, and healthcare-product organizations ensure that products comply with applicable regulatory requirements throughout their lifecycle."},{"type":"h","text":"The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Pharmaceutical Science","Regulation","Documentation","Quality","Business"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory research"},{"type":"h","text":"Product registration"},{"type":"h","text":"Dossier preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory submissions"},{"type":"h","text":"Application tracking"},{"type":"h","text":"Label and packaging review"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory correspondence"},{"type":"h","text":"Variation/change submissions"},{"type":"h","text":"Product renewals"},{"type":"h","text":"Compliance monitoring"},{"type":"h","text":"Coordination with quality, R&D, manufacturing and clinical teams"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory intelligence"},{"type":"h","text":"Submission lifecycle management"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Pharm graduate is well positioned because the degree provides foundational knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutics"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacology"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacognosy"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical pharmacy"},{"type":"h","text":"Drug formulation"},{"